{
  "kind": "a4-AGREEMENT-at-pool pilot (NOT a recall measurement)",
  "NOT_RECALL": "Every number in this file has a denominator made of 100% same-family LLM-judge verdicts: the pool's 'true facts' are the clusters one claude-sonnet-5 judge called GROUNDED_TRUE, and the judge was never calibrated against a mechanical oracle on this corpus. Per docs/design/95-benchmark-methodology.md (ratified) an uncalibrated same-family judge measures AGREEMENT, not truth, so these are agreement@pool(3) figures. Do NOT cite them as recall. The judge-free recall number for the four oracle-bearing shapes is harness/probes/adjudicate/calibration-report.a4-planted.{md,json} (planted edit-distance-1 mutations, labelled by an independent tsc oracle).",
  "AUDITABILITY_LIMIT": "adjudicated_clusters stores only {true, sources, shape} per cluster \u2014 NO fact text, no prompt, no per-call verdict log. The published tallies below re-derive EXACTLY from these rows by arithmetic (verified 2026-08-18), but no verdict in this file can be re-scored, re-judged or audited against the code it was about. Arithmetic-checkable, not adjudication-checkable.",
  "PRODUCER": "Hand-tallied from per-unit sub-agent runs; the producing driver is NOT recoverable from this repo. It was NOT harness/probes/a4-pool.mjs: that driver keyed its corpus on FILES and emitted {mode,modeNote,files,counts,atlasRun,pairCalls,adjudicated,recall}, while this artifact keys on path::symbol units and carries none of those fields; its own test declared live mode PENDING and out of scope. a4-pool.mjs + a4-pool.test.mjs + the two non-Atlas pool members were deleted on branch bench/results-honest; they remain in git history at commit b531755.",
  "method_doc": "docs/design/95a-recall-a4-methodology.md",
  "run_date": "2026-08-16",
